841	         `content_sha256` is the sha256 of the ORIGINAL bytes; an off-vocabulary region kind \
842	         (`paragraph`) and a `doc.v2` version are BOTH refused by the IR's loader, so the \
843	         closed vocabulary is a mechanism and not a word. Note what that hash IS, per the \
844	         crate's own correction of its plan: a PER-ACQUISITION dedup key, not a cross-retina \
845	         identity — a scan and an HTML page of one invoice have different bytes. For a \
846	         TOKENIZATION receipt that is exactly the right reading: you tokenize bytes, so \
847	         different bytes are a different tokenization, and cross-retina convergence is a facts \
848	         question (`converges_on_facts`) that is not this seam's business. Geometry is \
849	         `DomOrder` on both corpora because these are reading-order placements; claiming \
